Rendered a provider's settings in the order its driver asks for, and moved the driver choice to the top of the add form. The settings fieldset was built by walking the schema object as it arrived, which is alphabetical — `@identity-drivers` answers through plone.restapi, and that serialises an object with sorted keys — so an OIDC provider opened on "Attach to an existing account with the same verified email" and reached its issuer URL three fields later. Each field descriptor now carries its own position and the form sorts on that; a field that declares none sinks below those that do rather than disappearing.

The driver used to be the second question, under the provider ID. It decides which fields the form has at all, so it is the first one now — answering it is what makes the rest of the form exist. @ericof
